          "Under the US Foreign Corrupt Practices Act (FCPA) and the UK Bribery Act 2010, multinational corporations face crippling criminal penalties, executive imprisonment, and mandatory disgorgement of profits for paying bribes to foreign government officials. Crucially, companies are held criminally liable for bribes paid through third-party intermediaries—even if senior leadership claims lack of knowledge. Step 2: Record secondary accrual adjustment (710).",
